WEBVTT

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:08.890
One, two, three, four, two, two, three, four...

00:00:08.890 --> 00:00:10.770
Wassup!

00:00:13.310 --> 00:00:16.270
Yikes! Why no reaction?

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.220
Uh, wassup?

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:20.390
Broccoli!

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.100
I worked hard on that gag, and you ignore it?

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:28.720
Not only are you late, but your
jokes are leaving everyone cold.

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:33.470
Hurry up and stretch
before you freeze stiff.

00:00:33.470 --> 00:00:35.180
Broken broccoli!

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.180
Shall we slap some mayonnaise on it?

00:00:38.180 --> 00:00:40.310
Hey, guys, drop it! Hey!

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:42.350
What are you doing?

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.020
Gather round, everyone!

00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:49.770
Regarding our routine for the qualifiers,
I'd like to increase the difficulty of the stunts.

00:01:07.810 --> 00:01:13.470
<i>I'll put an end to spending</i>
<i>my days so thoughtlessly</i>

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:17.520
<i>I'm dying to break free of this</i>

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:23.220
<i>Since I can never take that first step forward,</i>

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:27.310
<i>you always take my hand and pull me along</i>

00:01:27.310 --> 00:01:33.140
<i>You've brought me to see</i>
<i>something completely new</i>

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.430
<i>My whole world is changing</i>

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.640
<i>With that first step</i>

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.810
<i>I felt transformed</i>

00:01:41.810 --> 00:01:46.810
<i>I can go anywhere; it'll work</i>
<i>out so long as we're together</i>

00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:48.390
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:01:48.390 --> 00:01:50.020
<i>just as you are</i>

00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:53.180
<i>At times you'll feel lost and scared,</i>

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:59.680
<i>but there are so many things you</i>
<i>won't know if you never give them a go</i>

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:01.310
<i>Go on, fly high, </i>

00:02:01.310 --> 00:02:06.180
<i>stretch out your hands until</i>
<i>you're almost touching the sky</i>

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:09.430
<i>We're not alone anymore</i>

00:02:09.430 --> 00:02:14.560
<i>Together we'll fly into a new world</i>

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:26.250
Caf Sunflower

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:27.100
We still haven't perfected our current formations,
and she wants to make things even harder?

00:02:27.100 --> 00:02:30.220
Doing harder stunts nets you more points.

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:31.600
What if you screw them up?

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:32.560
You lose points.

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.680
So it's the same as in figure skatin'.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:38.350
In that case, maybe we should
perfect the stunts we're already doing

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:42.520
instead of forcing ourselves to do hard ones.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.390
I know, right? Ain't it unreasonable
to make things even more difficult?

00:02:46.390 --> 00:02:48.720
How like you, Broccoli.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:52.220
Your spirit's been broken already.

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:55.770
Hey you, ever heard the phrase
"The mouth is the friend of misfortune"?

00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:58.640
You idiot, it's "The mouth
is the gate to misfortune."

00:02:58.640 --> 00:03:01.140
I... I just misspoke is all!

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:03.060
Hey now...

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:05.020
Ah, I knew you'd all be here.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:06.470
Kazu!

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:08.520
Practice is already over.

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.560
Sorry, my tutoring job went on forever.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.470
The middle school students I'm teaching
are taking their entrance exams soon.

00:03:14.470 --> 00:03:17.680
Really? Entrance exams
are serious, very serious.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.890
Mizo, you failed them twice, right?

00:03:19.890 --> 00:03:22.020
You're more senior than us!

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.430
So you both passed on your first try...

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:31.310
Great timing. We're discussing whether
to increase the difficulty of our stunts.

00:03:31.310 --> 00:03:33.810
The coach told us to decide ourselves.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:36.520
Well, isn't this a great challenge?

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:38.100
It sure is!

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.350
Of course!

00:03:39.350 --> 00:03:44.020
Huh? Let's not get carried away
and just enjoy performing!

00:03:44.020 --> 00:03:46.470
But we want to pass
the qualifiers, don't we?

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:51.390
Then wouldn't it be better
to perfect our current routine?

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:54.180
Tono, you're too defeatist.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:03:58.680
Just who the hell do you think you are?!

00:03:58.680 --> 00:04:03.970
Look here, you two. We're having a discussion,
so it's natural to hear lots of different opinions, no?

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:06.810
Haru's right.

00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:12.180
I want us to challenge ourselves. But if we all
aren't willing to do that, then we shouldn't.

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:17.180
That's true. If we do this half-heartedly,
someone will just get hurt.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:17.810
So...

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:19.060
What is it, Takumi?

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:24.310
Well, like Takeru said, if I get to
enjoy performing, then I'm fine with that.

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:28.970
I saw you guys have so much fun dancing,
and thought that I wanted to be a part of that.

00:04:28.970 --> 00:04:31.850
Besides, realistically speaking,
it would be hard for some of us.

00:04:31.850 --> 00:04:32.810
Why's that?

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:38.140
My brother and Kin are third-years,
so they've started job-hunting...

00:04:38.140 --> 00:04:40.180
It's been quite an ordeal.

00:04:40.180 --> 00:04:43.100
Oh, so that's why they took today off?

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:47.020
The harder the stunts,
the more we'll have to practice.

00:04:47.020 --> 00:04:51.140
But, in order to pass the qualifiers,
don't we want to raise the bar?

00:04:51.140 --> 00:04:54.020
How 'bout we get the whole team together?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.520
Everyone with a part-time job
can't possibly practice more than this.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:04.020
Right, let's see how things go for a little bit
longer and then make our decision.

00:05:04.020 --> 00:05:04.970
You okay with that?

00:05:04.970 --> 00:05:07.180
We need to decide by the end of the year.

00:05:07.180 --> 00:05:10.890
If we're going to do it, then I'd like
to start practicing right after New Year's.

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:15.430
♪ Cho-co-late parfait! ♪

00:05:15.430 --> 00:05:20.350
If only everyone could cheer up
with a parfait like you.

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:24.680
Today was super awkward again,
wasn't it? All thanks to him.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:27.350
Takeru, this is your fault, too.

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.310
Even if he pisses you off,
you gotta have a little self-control.

00:05:30.310 --> 00:05:33.930
If we all practice hard, then
everybody's mood will improve.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:36.890
That's a very sports club way of thinkin'!

00:05:36.890 --> 00:05:39.020
What're ya fakin' that accent for?

00:05:39.020 --> 00:05:41.100
Doncha think I sound great?

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.270
Who are you, Chen?

00:05:44.970 --> 00:05:46.810
Come on i--

00:05:46.810 --> 00:05:47.810
Takuya and...

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:48.600
Yo!

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:49.640
...Kin?!

00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:50.850
Two black coffees.

00:05:50.850 --> 00:05:53.310
Uh, right.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:55.520
I heard you guys started lookin' for work.

00:05:55.520 --> 00:05:59.350
Some financial companies had a joint job fair.

00:05:59.350 --> 00:06:03.390
I want to go into banking, and Kin
wants to go into damage insurance.

00:06:03.390 --> 00:06:04.520
How stuffy...

00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:06.560
Our futures are shrouded in darkness.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:11.850
As a man, for my life's work, I'd like
to follow up on people's lives.

00:06:11.850 --> 00:06:14.850
Your statement of purpose is perfect.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:18.600
Kin, Takuya. Um, about practice...

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:21.600
Captain, I'm sorry I had to take today off.

00:06:21.600 --> 00:06:22.520
Here you go.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.520
Much appreciated.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:27.060
We'll try hard to practice and
find jobs before the tournament!

00:06:29.810 --> 00:06:34.100
I see... Kin and Takuya both have it tough.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:38.770
Seems like Sho couldn't bring himself
to say "Don't skip practice," too.

00:06:38.770 --> 00:06:40.100
Kazu?

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:42.770
Sorry. I can't go to practice today, either.

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:44.270
What? You have work?

00:06:44.270 --> 00:06:48.890
No, I have to go to my grandma's hospital.

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:52.600
Ah, for payments and procedures and stuff.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:56.310
I know everyone's worried, but...

00:06:56.310 --> 00:06:57.310
You're right.

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.680
Do me this favor, Haru.

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:00.680
Yeah, I got it.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.930
Saku, don't look down!
And keep your knees straight!

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:12.560
When you bend your upper body,
the bases drift apart.

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:15.720
That makes you unstable,
which strains their backs.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:19.220
Really? So that's why
Takumi said his back hurt.

00:07:19.220 --> 00:07:20.640
Is that why he took today off?

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:24.680
He hurt himself because he hasn't
built up his abdominal or back muscles.

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:28.060
My brother has been
training properly with me.

00:07:28.060 --> 00:07:33.720
Then you should both make sure
he stays in good shape.

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:43.470
Y'know, back when I did judo,
I heard that a lot.

00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:47.720
That I didn't have any muscle, or that keeping
in shape was just as important as practicing.

00:07:47.720 --> 00:07:49.020
From my big sister.

00:07:49.020 --> 00:07:50.560
You did judo?

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:52.350
Are you a black belt?

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:53.680
Well, more or less.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:55.140
And you have an older sister?

00:07:55.140 --> 00:07:57.100
Older's fine by me!

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:01.390
Can we leave this repugnant, unproductive
conversation at that and get back to practice?

00:08:01.390 --> 00:08:03.220
Uh, sure.

00:08:05.140 --> 00:08:06.520
Let's do this.

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:08.390
Yuuup.

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:12.680
Is Kazu working today, too?

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:15.890
No, he said he was seeing
his grandma at the hospital.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:19.310
Kazu's grandma was hospitalized.

00:08:19.310 --> 00:08:20.640
I had no idea...

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:22.720
What a great guy he is.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.310
A stellar student with a
scholarship who does cheerleading,

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:28.770
and on top of that, he works
part-time and visits his grandma.

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:31.430
And despite everything
he never, ever complains.

00:08:31.430 --> 00:08:33.770
Haru, which hospital is it?

00:08:33.770 --> 00:08:36.220
The one between Iidabashi and Kagurazaka.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:39.770
I wonder if we could go visit her, too.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:40.890
Shall we?

00:08:40.890 --> 00:08:45.270
Family's important. This is another
follow-up on someone's life.

00:08:45.270 --> 00:08:46.770
I am a bit worried.

00:08:46.770 --> 00:08:48.600
Then I'm going, too!

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:52.060
All right, I'll ask Kazu about it.

00:08:52.060 --> 00:08:55.470
Haruki, there's something I need to tell you.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.520
I'm quitting the Breakers.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:02.060
Quitting?!

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:06.020
Normally I would have told Kazuma,
but he's not here today.

