00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:33.600
Haru!

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:34.560
Hey.

00:11:34.560 --> 00:11:38.680
Sorry I'm so late. I should've
given you a spare key.

00:11:38.680 --> 00:11:40.810
I'm not your girlfriend.

00:11:43.100 --> 00:11:46.310
So why'd you want
to talk all of a sudden?

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:49.470
Wait, is it her? Did something
happen with Chihiro?

00:11:49.470 --> 00:11:51.520
No!

00:11:51.520 --> 00:11:53.220
I got a message from Saku earlier.

00:11:53.220 --> 00:11:54.180
Yeah.

00:11:54.180 --> 00:11:57.810
That was my fault. I'd only typed "I."

00:11:57.810 --> 00:11:58.680
"I"?

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:03.810
I meant to type "I haven't
heard yet," but I was in a rush.

00:12:03.810 --> 00:12:09.310
No, it's my fault. Everyone came
because they were worried, and I...

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:11.850
Is your grandma okay?

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:14.270
Yeah, she's feeling great!

00:12:14.270 --> 00:12:17.640
Man, when I'm there she talks
non-stop and won't let me leave!

00:12:17.640 --> 00:12:21.430
So lately, I've been going there a lot.

00:12:21.430 --> 00:12:23.930
I see.

00:12:23.930 --> 00:12:26.310
That's not all you wanted
to talk about, right?

00:12:26.310 --> 00:12:27.430
Uh, no.

00:12:27.430 --> 00:12:28.720
What's up?

00:12:28.720 --> 00:12:30.310
It's Hisashi.

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:36.060
Hisashi said he's going
to quit the Breakers.

00:12:36.060 --> 00:12:37.560
How sudden.

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:39.520
It ain't sudden at all.

00:12:39.520 --> 00:12:41.430
Did you let him, Kazu?

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:44.640
Oh, I'm the one who heard from Hisashi.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:46.350
You tried to stop him, right?

00:12:46.350 --> 00:12:47.430
Yes.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.970
But it was no good?

00:12:49.970 --> 00:12:51.890
Nothing we can do.

00:12:51.890 --> 00:12:57.310
Well, with him gone, this awkward
atmosphere will clear right up, won't it?

00:12:57.310 --> 00:12:59.770
This is for the best.

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:00.680
I wonder.

00:13:00.680 --> 00:13:01.970
Wonder what?

00:13:01.970 --> 00:13:03.770
Is Hisashi leaving really okay?

00:13:03.770 --> 00:13:07.720
He was always the first person to arrive...

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:12.060
...and the first one to report
how much he'd practiced.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:16.810
He had such high hopes
for the Breakers, and yet...

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:18.600
Um...

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:20.430
Hisashi, he...

00:13:20.430 --> 00:13:25.270
He's actually always kept me
company while I've practiced.

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:27.930
But he was so harsh with you!

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:34.060
He was trying to encourage me.
He just has a sharp tongue.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:39.600
When Hisashi told me I was giving up,
I knew he was right, and so...

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:45.890
After practice ended, I spent
a long time training by myself.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:47.680
And then...

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:52.600
You should straighten up your back more.

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:58.470
And he's been watching everyone so closely.

00:13:58.470 --> 00:14:03.850
The only member of the Breakers
who's decent at cheerleading is Sho.

00:14:03.850 --> 00:14:07.970
Kazu is almost there, and Haru,
Ichiro, and Gen will get there

00:14:07.970 --> 00:14:11.270
one way or another, with their athletic talent.

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:15.220
"Mizoguchi doesn't have enough flexibility.

00:14:15.220 --> 00:14:19.100
Kin doesn't have any either,
but he sticks to the basics.

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:24.270
Gin and Doh don't have much stamina
or muscle, but they have incredible focus.

00:14:24.270 --> 00:14:29.180
The Nabeshima brothers' dance is wonderful.
I don't have that kind of rhythm myself,

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:31.640
so I'd love to take the time to learn it.

00:14:31.640 --> 00:14:36.810
Chen will be fine. Sakuma just
needs to put his heart into it.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.430
As for Ando..."

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:41.470
While his attitude toward
practice needs some work,

00:14:41.470 --> 00:14:45.350
he gets really serious when he's working as a base.

00:14:45.350 --> 00:14:48.600
I think he's committed to it, but...

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:54.560
Whenever I see his goofy face,
I just fly off the handle.

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:55.430
Still,

00:14:55.430 --> 00:14:58.310
I'm sure everyone can work even harder!

00:14:58.310 --> 00:15:02.220
I know the Breakers can
become an even better team!

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:09.520
Hisashi gave our team
considerable thought.

00:15:09.520 --> 00:15:10.680
Seriously?

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.930
It's so hard to get what he's thinking.

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:16.640
He's simply a somewhat
harsh but passionate man.

00:15:16.640 --> 00:15:17.810
Right!

00:15:17.810 --> 00:15:21.680
Bro, we still haven't taught
Hisashi our dance yet!

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:22.890
Yeah!

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:27.680
I guess the Breakers need Hisashi.

00:15:27.680 --> 00:15:30.270
Yeah, let's all bring him back!

00:15:30.270 --> 00:15:32.600
I wonder where he is right now?

00:15:32.600 --> 00:15:40.180
Well, I promised to train with
Hisashi again after practice today.

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:41.720
You serious?

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:46.520
Thanks for taking the trouble to come.

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:50.140
Well, a promise is a promise.

00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:55.470
I heard you said you're
quitting the Breakers today.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:59.970
And yet you still came
to practice with me.

00:15:59.970 --> 00:16:01.390
Shall we begin?

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:04.220
Yeah, let's get started.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:06.350
With all of us together!

00:16:06.350 --> 00:16:09.180
All right, let's start with some stretches!

00:16:09.180 --> 00:16:13.180
Hey, wait, what's going on?
I told Haru I was quitting--

00:16:13.180 --> 00:16:17.640
You said no, but your heart says yes, right?

00:16:17.640 --> 00:16:20.970
The Breakers need you, Hisashi.

00:16:20.970 --> 00:16:25.060
We don't have anyone who's
as hard on us as you are!

00:16:27.140 --> 00:16:28.890
You say sumthin', too.

00:16:30.970 --> 00:16:37.560
Well, it's true. If the water's lukewarm, you gotta
turn up the heat to boil some tasty broccoli.

00:16:37.560 --> 00:16:39.930
Broccoli!

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:46.720
I don't care if you boil it, stew it, or grill it--
I don't think you can enjoy broccoli at all.

00:16:46.720 --> 00:16:49.270
Now that's just being picky.

00:16:49.270 --> 00:16:51.810
A man isn't fussy about his food.

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:58.470
So, let's start practicing. We've decided to
increase the complexity of our stunts, after all.

00:16:58.470 --> 00:16:59.640
What?

00:16:59.640 --> 00:17:02.390
Don't you want to stand out
and show 'em how cool we are?

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:06.270
And on the days we have to go job hunting,
we'll practice in the morning.

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:11.850
Won't you come back, Hisashi?

00:17:14.310 --> 00:17:19.390
I... actually wanted to be
on Yomei's team, Sparks.

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.970
But I failed Yomei's entrance exam.

00:17:24.970 --> 00:17:29.310
And I thought I wouldn't be able
to do cheerleading anymore.

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:35.810
So when I heard that this university
had a cheerleading club for men...

00:17:35.810 --> 00:17:40.430
I was so very happy. That's why...

00:17:40.430 --> 00:17:41.810
S'all good.

00:17:41.810 --> 00:17:43.720
More importantly, let's get practicin'!

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:46.640
Let me join your solo practice sessions, too!

00:17:49.640 --> 00:17:52.640
All right, we'll practice all winter break!

00:17:52.640 --> 00:17:53.680
Yeah!

00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:56.520
Speaking of which, I put in an
application for us to train together

00:17:56.520 --> 00:18:00.180
at one of our university's
seminar houses through the New Year.

00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:09.890
Thank you very much for touring
with the Breakers today.

00:18:09.890 --> 00:18:11.720
We will now pass through the
Tokyo Metropolitan Expressway,

00:18:11.720 --> 00:18:14.020
travel along the Eastern Kanto
Expressway, and then head for

00:18:14.020 --> 00:18:16.180
the Hasaki seminar house.

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:22.020
So for approximately the next two and a half
hours, you get to listen to my beautiful voice!

00:18:23.680 --> 00:18:25.470
What's so beautiful about it?

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:27.810
I'd prefer a screechin' crow!

00:18:27.810 --> 00:18:30.770
Caw, caw!

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:32.270
Okay, I'm gonna sing!

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:35.220
No, let's play Truth or Dare!

00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:37.100
What is this, a slumber party?

00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:39.140
How about a drinking game?

00:18:39.140 --> 00:18:40.930
Oh, that sounds like fun!

00:18:40.930 --> 00:18:42.640
Let me sleep.

00:18:42.640 --> 00:18:43.810
We're sorry!

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:45.850
Everyone's acting like a bunch of kids.

00:18:45.850 --> 00:18:48.310
Reminds me of our elementary school outings.

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:53.930
Well, once we arrive, it's strictly practice.
This is probably their only chance to enjoy themselves.

00:18:55.140 --> 00:18:57.470
Hisashi? Are you all right?

00:18:57.470 --> 00:18:58.850
Are you carsick?

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:00.430
Come sit in the front!

00:19:00.430 --> 00:19:05.470
--A bag! Get a bag! Hurry!
--It's the dried squid in vinegar! Stay away from me!

00:19:09.220 --> 00:19:13.140
All right, starting today, we're practicing
with the new stunts we added.

00:19:13.140 --> 00:19:17.220
We thought up a secret
weapon with the coach.

00:19:17.220 --> 00:19:18.720
Secret weapon?

00:19:18.720 --> 00:19:20.270
Sounds impressive.

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:22.390
Now, let's begin!

00:20:21.770 --> 00:20:23.180
It's finally done.

00:20:23.180 --> 00:20:25.720
A lightly sweetened soup fit for a man.

00:20:25.720 --> 00:20:28.430
This'll finish boiling soon.
How's the seasoning?

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:29.850
I'm on it!

00:20:29.850 --> 00:20:32.810
Oh, you've minced them beautifully.

00:20:35.390 --> 00:20:37.310
This is so, so tasty.

00:20:37.310 --> 00:20:40.100
The soup is beyond good.

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:42.020
It's our Big Bro's specialty!

00:20:42.020 --> 00:20:43.930
You did a great job.

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:46.350
I wonder if the temple bell
will stop ringing soon.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.310
It's tolled 87 times now.

00:20:48.310 --> 00:20:50.060
Not bad, Bro!

00:20:50.060 --> 00:20:52.350
Once we're done eating, we'll do
our first shrine visit of the year!

00:20:52.350 --> 00:20:54.270
I want to see the sunrise, too.

00:20:54.270 --> 00:20:55.430
Yeah!

00:21:01.390 --> 00:21:05.600
Come to think of it, didn't you and I
watch the first sunrise together last year?

00:21:05.600 --> 00:21:07.350
Up on your roof.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:13.600
How strange, last year I'd have never imagined
we'd be watching it here with everyone.

00:21:13.600 --> 00:21:15.520
All right, here we go!

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:17.220
Go, fight, win!

00:21:17.220 --> 00:21:18.850
Let's go, Br--

00:21:18.850 --> 00:21:21.020
Broccoli!

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:24.270
Why ya gotta say that on New Year's?

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:26.310
You're ruinin' the moment!

00:21:26.310 --> 00:21:29.520
Huh? I was just trying
to make everyone laugh.

00:21:29.520 --> 00:21:31.930
Let's start over.

00:21:31.930 --> 00:21:33.680
All right, here we go!

00:21:33.680 --> 00:21:35.310
Go, fight, win!

00:21:35.310 --> 00:21:36.930
Let's go, Br--

00:21:36.930 --> 00:21:38.520
Broccoli!

00:21:42.350 --> 00:21:43.890
Hisashi, he's...

00:21:43.890 --> 00:21:46.220
...broken down.

00:21:46.220 --> 00:21:47.770
No.

00:21:47.770 --> 00:21:50.600
You've broken down your
former self, haven't you?

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:56.890
--Yes, yes, yes, yes!
--Now Hisashi is a full-fledged Breaker, too!

00:22:05.220 --> 00:22:07.810
Our routine is two minutes, 30 seconds.

00:22:07.810 --> 00:22:09.720
A mere 150 seconds.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:13.680
In those moments, let's leave
the other teams lost for words!

00:22:13.680 --> 00:22:15.220
Right!

00:22:17.970 --> 00:22:21.970
The Dawning of a Bond

00:22:31.930 --> 00:22:35.470
<i>Without even thinking, I shouted a reply</i>

00:22:35.470 --> 00:22:42.100
<i>The voice opening that new door</i>
<i>sounded like a tightly clenched fist</i>

00:22:42.100 --> 00:22:45.520
<i>Resounding with reassuring determination</i>

00:22:45.520 --> 00:22:48.890
<i>I think if I let out</i>
<i>(I've been waiting for this)</i>

00:22:48.890 --> 00:22:52.180
<i>All my pent-up energy</i>
<i>(I can change something)</i>

00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:58.770
<i>We've always been looking for</i>
<i>something this cool! Ain't that right?</i>

00:22:58.770 --> 00:23:01.680
<i>Feeling insecure</i>
<i>(Oh my God!)</i>

00:23:01.680 --> 00:23:04.970
<i>I fell into a funk</i>
<i>(Oh my pride!)</i>

00:23:04.970 --> 00:23:07.060
<i>Send that old me</i>
<i>(Don't give in!)</i>

00:23:07.060 --> 00:23:08.720
<i>A solid cheer</i>
<i>(Go, go!)</i>

00:23:08.720 --> 00:23:13.220
<i>Make encouraging motions</i>
<i>(Let's dance together!)</i>

00:23:13.220 --> 00:23:16.600
<i>Yes! Fly high, fly dive, up and away!</i>

00:23:16.600 --> 00:23:20.350
<i>Never hang your head and give up</i>
<i>(No!) </i>

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:23.680
<i>Break up, break out, break it to smithereens</i>
<i>(Yes!)</i>

00:23:23.680 --> 00:23:26.970
<i>Smile together, break a sweat, show your guts!</i>
<i>(Guts!)</i>

00:23:26.970 --> 00:23:33.600
<i>Strike a victory pose toward the blue sky</i>
<i>(Jump! Jump! High V!)</i>

00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:36.770
<i>Win over everybody's hearts!</i>

00:23:36.770 --> 00:23:40.140
<i>Go for that moment when</i>
<i>you meet a sparkling smile</i>

00:23:43.470 --> 00:23:48.270
<i>Go, fight! Go, fight, win!</i>

00:23:52.520 --> 00:23:54.220
Kazu's taking today off?

00:23:54.220 --> 00:23:57.350
This is an unprecedented event.
It has to be love.

00:23:57.350 --> 00:23:58.600
I know how he feels.

00:23:58.600 --> 00:23:59.390
Big Bro!

00:23:59.390 --> 00:24:01.680
Maybe it isn't going well.

00:24:01.680 --> 00:24:03.100
She broke his heart?

00:24:03.100 --> 00:24:05.350
Let's not jump to conclusions here.

00:24:05.350 --> 00:24:09.960
Next Episode: Tears of the Sun.

00:24:05.720 --> 00:24:08.350
Next Episode: Tears of the Sun.

00:24:08.350 --> 00:24:09.970
Go! Fight! Win!
